===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[confidence|Confidence]] in or [[reliance]] on some person or quality.
#: {{ux|en|He needs to regain her '''trust''' if he is ever going to win her back.}}
#: {{ux|en|to lose '''trust''' in someone}}
#: {{ux|en|build up '''trust'''}}
#: {{ux|en|a relationship built on mutual '''trust'''}}
#* {{RQ:Locke Human Understanding|I|text=taking things upon '''trust'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1671|author=w:John Milton|title=w:Samson Agonistes
|passage=O ever-failing '''trust''' / In mortal strength!}}
# [[dependence|Dependence]] upon something in the future; [[hope]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|2 Corinthians|3|4|passage=Such '''trust''' have we through Christ.}}
# Confidence in the future payment for goods or services supplied; [[credit]].
#: {{ux|en|I was out of cash, but the landlady let me have it on '''trust'''.}}
# That which is committed or entrusted; something received in confidence; a charge.
# That upon which confidence is reposed; ground of reliance; hope.
#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=Psalms|chapter=71|verse=5|passage=O Lord God, thou art my '''trust''' from my youth.}}
# {{lb|en|rare}} [[trustworthiness|Trustworthiness]], [[reliability]].
# The condition or obligation of one to whom anything is confided; responsible charge or office.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear|act=I|scene=iv|passage=I do profess to be no less than I seem; to serve him truly that<br>will put me in '''trust'''}}
#* '''17th century''', {{w|John Denham (poet)|John Denham}}, ''Of Justice''
#*: Reward them well, if they observe their '''trust'''.
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[confidence]] vested in a person who has legal ownership of a property to manage for the benefit of another.
#: {{ux|en|I put the house into my sister's '''trust'''.}}
# {{lb|en|trust law}} An arrangement whereby property or money is given to be held by a third party (a [[trustee]]), on the basis that it will be managed for the benefit of, or eventually transferred to, a stated [[beneficiary]]; for example, money to be given to a child when he or she reaches adulthood.
# A group of businessmen or traders organised for mutual benefit to produce and distribute specific commodities or services, and managed by a central body of [[trustees]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} Affirmation of the [[access]] [[right]]s of a [[user]] of a computer system.

